    gas_commitment_bridge: { cell: "U", ev: "miso-130 DESCRIPTIVE pool census, NO prereg, cell stays U: model CC day-anchored night-off plants in July = 3 / 1,601 MW (2023), 0 / 0 MW (2024, 2025) — model CCs already run near-flat through summer nights (17.8–18.8 GW night vs 18.5–20.0 GW day), the same shape as PJM's kill; a future MISO charter must confront this census in its own PRE-REGISTERED pre-check (FINDING-miso130-c7-night-regime-2026-08-05.md §5). miso-133 adds the SLACK side of the same census, also DESCRIPTIVE (PREREG §2 S-4 declared it ungated, so the cell stays U and NO verdict is taken from it): at July night the keeper dispatches 6.1 % of assembled CT_PEAKER and 16.9 % of ST_GAS, leaving ~41 GW of idle non-coal gas capability against a 3.2 GW (2025) non-coal shortfall — CT_PEAKER availability would have to fall to ~20 % before its idle block alone stopped covering the whole shortfall. A bridge adds CAPABILITY, and MISO's overnight capability is ~10× the shortfall and idle, so the mechanism could not bind even if the pool were full (FINDING-miso133-overnight-identity-basis-2026-08-05.md §6)" },
