    seam_flow_envelopes: { cell: "K", ev: "HOUR-KEY REPAIRED 2026-08-22 (miso-175, keeper 2026-08-22-miso-175-hourkey): the envelope's (month x hod) bucketing now reads local_time as hour-ENDING under miso_seam_envelope_hour_ending_key (armed on the keeper), closing the +1 h rotation miso-174 §4 found — cell stays K, STRENGTHENED (see the miso_seam_envelope_hour_ending_key row). PRIOR EV FOLLOWS: keeper (miso_seam_flow_limit + miso_seam_export_limit + miso_seam_envelope_merit_cap + miso_seam_measured_ladder + miso_manitoba_seam, all armed on 2026-08-04-miso-122b-scope-gate). CELL STAYS K AND IS STRENGTHENED, no verdict minted, no re-solve: miso-123 (2026-08-04, no LP) measured the armed p90 envelope's own hour-of-day FIDELITY for the first time and it is high — the cap's 24-point hod profile tracks the MEASURED directed BA-to-BA flow at r = +0.952/+0.987/+0.955 (PJM), +0.904/+0.973/+0.948 (SPP), +0.814/+0.837/+0.844 (South), +0.996/+0.992/+0.986 (Manitoba) across 2023/24/25, while the model's cleared flow tracks it at -0.638/-0.753/-0.852 (PJM). The envelope family is therefore EXONERATED of MISO's seam hour-of-day defect: it is the one channel already carrying the measured shape, and the defect sits on the hour-INVARIANT price ladder instead (see the import_shape_lever row, MISO cell G). Two by-products reported, not armed: the envelope's marginal binding share on PJM is 0.6/2.4/1.4 % overnight vs 12.0/28.6/11.6 % at peak (so the cap shapes the peak limb only), and an offline reconstruction of the seam bands from these objects against the keeper's own solved P1 duals reproduces the keeper's solved import class at r = +0.994/+0.995/+0.993 with a -38/-25/-19 MW bias — an independent check that the armed family behaves as its docstrings describe. DO NOT re-derive the envelope statistic or sweep miso_seam_flow_percentile against the hod residual (rule 23 [R-FROZEN-DERIVE]); miso-123 §5 bounds the entire availability-ceiling class out of that job." },
