    economic_retirement_screen: { cell: "R", fc: "R", ev: "ff-verdicts FC-3; RC-1A-D1; FFR-2B (runs miso-2021-2025-cmc-{legacy,pipeline}-ffr2b); FFR-3C (docs/handoffs/ffr-3c-collapse-attribution-2026-08-03.md §1/§3.2 — MISO T1-F paired arms, zero economic exits both arms); FFR-3A-2 (docs/handoffs/ffr-3a2-battery-close-2026-08-03.md §3.9 — run miso-2021-2025-ffr3a2: ALL THREE retirement bands flip FAIL→PASS (total 10.814→13.734 vs 15.227 actual, recall, false_retire); coal 1.387→12.95, gas_st 8.643→0.0; FC-3 now fails on the ADDITIONS half alone); FFR-3A-3 (docs/handoffs/ffr-3a3-battery-close-2026-08-04.md §2.5/§3/§5 — run miso-2021-2025-realized-ffr3a3 RE-MEASURES THAT SAME LEG at the post-FFR-3F HEAD 941f4983 with the UNCONDITIONAL G3 cap-grain fix 2adfb49, and the FFR-3A-2 sweep does NOT survive it: retire.total_gw 13.734 PASS → 12.716 FAIL (−16.5% vs 15.227 actual), so §3.9's headline 'every retirement band now PASSES' is 2/3 POST-FIX, NOT 3/3. recall PASS 13/17 and false_retire PASS 0.997 GW both unchanged; coal economic 12.95→11.932 GW, announced nuclear 0.768 / biomass 0.016 unmoved. The post-fix coal 11.932 GW, false-retire 0.997 GW and recall 13/17 are EXACTLY FFR-2B's paired-control values — CONVERGENCE, NOT ATTRIBUTION (no control arm ran here). Read with PJM, two ISOs land independently on controlled values, so the pre-fix figures carried the grain bug and in MISO's case it FLATTERED a level band into a PASS. DIRECTION IS NOT SHARED WITH PJM: MISO UNDER-retires (12.716 vs 15.227) where PJM OVER-retires, so one throughput story will not explain both. CELL UNCHANGED, determination UNMOVED (HOLD)); FFR-3A-4 (results/ffr3a4/RESULT-miso-t1x-2026-08-04.md; run miso-2023-2027-crossover-ffr3a4, cache key 46954f417b6e18e2 — the T1-X leg FFR-3A-3 launched twice and lost twice to OOM, now MEASURED. **A STRUCTURAL NULL, AND MISO'S CROSSOVER IS THEREFORE INCAPABLE OF TESTING THIS RULE.** The evolution ledgers execute ZERO economic retirements in 2023, 2024 AND 2025 and land 3 exits / 432.8 MW in 2026 — a year SOLVED BUT NEVER SCORED (rule 22) — so a fix to the screen's ADMISSION set has nothing to act on inside the scored window. All 10 banded metrics consequently reproduce the pre-fix comparator miso-2023-2027-crossover-ffr3a2 to 3 d.p. (delta +0.0000 on every row), and the determination is HOLD, unchanged. This independently reproduces IN MISO the pattern FFR-3L established for ERCOT's crossover, on MISO's OWN evidence (rule 25 clean, nothing imported). It also resolves why MISO's T1-H moved MOST of the four legs while its T1-X does not move at all: T1-H seeds from 2020 over 2021-2025 and executes exits inside its scored window, T1-X seeds from the 2023 vintage over 2023-2027 and does not — same fix, different decision set, different fleet, exactly the PJM precedent. NO VERDICT MINTED AND THE CELL STAYS R: a null by construction is evidence for neither rule (the FFR-3C §3.2 pattern), no control arm ran, and no future session should attribute a scored MISO T1-X movement to the retirement rule. Prediction PRE-REGISTERED before the bundle existed and the discriminating ledger check fixed in advance — see results/ffr3a4/PREREG-miso-t1x-2026-08-04.md, committed at 00b0637c)" },
